{
  "dom_id": "step-q134266",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "An antique broker has records about the value of an artwork $y$ (in thousands of dollars) at certain times $x$ (in decades) since the artwork was produced. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=3.2x+4.5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the residual $5$ decades after the artwork was produced if the actual value of the artwork after $5$ decades is $$23\\,000?$",
  "worked_solution": "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the estimated value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =3.2x+4.5 \\\\  & =3.2(5)+4.5 \\\\  & =20.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =23-20.5 \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $$2\\,500.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
